// AiXenix Cosmos Lab web client: place a catalogue body preset into the live world. The preset's scene-body record is
// cloned (its catalogue attributes and looks preserved), given a unique key, name, mass and radius, and placed on a
// circular (or chosen-speed) orbit around a primary: position and velocity are computed in SI here and sent as the
// scene schema's top-level position_m / velocity_mps. The engine (core scene parser + AddBody) stays the authority for
// overlap, capacity and validity; a refusal leaves the world unchanged and keeps this dialog open.

